  "worked_solution": "The denominators are $3$ and $6.$ We can make a common denominator of $6.$\n\n We split the shape on the left of the division sign into $2$ parts horizontally:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14153326/assets/8dd0573a6eb88df56d6cec9ef5bd819a429a936609bd51d9fc4ba0e9968e5ef9.png)\n\nSo, our division problem now is\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{6}÷\\frac{5}{6}.\n$$\n\nSince the denominators are equal, this is equivalent to\n\n$$\n4÷5=\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}÷\\frac{5}{6}=\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$",
